X/GUI APPS WORK IN-BROWSER (sandcastle, 2026-05-29). Witnessed live: GUI app on the desktop renders an in-guest x86_64 window (blue title bar/green/orange content/gradient bg) drawn by containers/xappdemo.elf under blink, on a canvas, no server. THREE bugs fixed to get here: (1) xappdemo _start must be NAKED asm capturing rsp then tail-call main(argc,argv) -- a normal C function's prologue mangles rsp so argv read garbage (commit 86b6a7d). (2) blink SpyAddress/LookupAddress2 is PER-PAGE (returns host ptr valid only for the 4KB page containing vaddr; guest mmap pages are non-contiguous in host mem) -- fbView must assemble the framebuffer page-by-page via spy_address(base+off) per 4096 bytes; reading stride*height contiguously goes black past page 0 (webix af6318a). (3) blink runs ONE elf at a time (runElf 'previous run not yet settled') -- serialize ALL VM work through client-sandbox-store.runExclusive (per-workspace promise chain) + single-flight tick + activePumps strict-mode dedupe; GUI uses render-once (run one frame, blit, exit; host re-runs on input) since runElf is synchronous. portabox Sandbox.displayPixels() returns the page-assembled RGBA buffer (b08ce18). xappdemo.elf working build = 9456 bytes (NOT the stale 21599). dev server: kill ALL next-server before restart or .next write-batch race hangs /desktop; if 3000 held it uses 3003. Commits: webix af6318a (fbView page-walk)+86b6a7d (naked start), portabox b08ce18 (displayPixels), sandcastle 3161378+01c2913 (GuiDesktopApp+runExclusive). A full Xorg/X11 server is still impractical under single-thread NOJIT blink; this fbdev-direct GUI app is the working display producer.